  <div class="tale-introduction"><p class="eyebrow">A MISSION TO FIND SITA</p><p>Ravana has abducted Sita. Rama and his brother Lakshmana have allied with Sugriva, whose vanaras search for her. This condensed retelling follows the <strong>Sundara Kanda of the Valmiki Ramayana</strong>, from Hanuman’s crossing to his return with news. It is original English prose, rather than a verse-by-verse translation.</p></div>
  <section aria-labelledby="characters-title" class="story-characters"><p class="eyebrow">MEET THE CHARACTERS</p><h2 id="characters-title">Characters in this story</h2><dl>
    <div><dt>Hanuman</dt><dd>Son of the Wind-god, Sugriva’s minister and Rama’s messenger.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Sita</dt><dd>Rama’s wife, held captive in Lanka and steadfast under threat.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Rama &amp; Lakshmana</dt><dd>The brothers awaiting news of Sita.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Sugriva</dt><dd>The vanara king whose search parties seek Sita.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Ravana</dt><dd>The ruler of Lanka who has abducted Sita.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Vibhishana</dt><dd>Ravana’s brother, who argues against killing an envoy.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Indrajit</dt><dd>Ravana’s warrior son, who captures Hanuman.</dd></div>
    <div><dt>Jambavan &amp; Angada</dt><dd>Leaders among the companions awaiting Hanuman’s return.</dd></div>
